From eea4028e25ea995baf0ff9f69b3094914efd4140 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 18:26:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add four scroll reveal variants: rise, blur, mask, lines
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extends the single fade-up ScrollReveal into a small system with four
flavours, so text, photos and video each animate as what they are
instead of all reaching for the same treatment:

- rise: the original — opacity + a lift. Stays the fallback for any
  data-animate="true" section that carries no more specific marker,
  exactly as before, and is used explicitly for cards, stats, list
  rows and small labels.
- blur: a photograph settling into focus (a shorter lift, filter
  blur to sharp) — gallery thumbnails, project covers, team and bio
  photos, before/after pairs.
- mask: an edge-to-edge banner unveiled with a rising clip-path
  rather than faded — the single video-loop block, the media block's
  own full-bleed default variant, the case-study hero image, and the
  default hero's cover.
- lines: a heading split into its own lines (GSAP SplitText) and
  lifted in one at a time — case-study narrative copy and pull
  quotes/testimonials.

All four share the site's one easing and pull their distances and
timings from the existing duration/stagger/revealDistance tokens
(plus one new one, revealBlur, for the blur radius) — no scale, no
rotation, same restraint the tokens already documented. CMS-authored
blocks (MediaBlock, TeamBlock, BioBlock, TestimonialBlock) still gate
on the editor's own settings.animate toggle; only elements that opt
in with an explicit data-reveal, or the section-level fallback, ever
move.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
